# Smallfloat scalar byte load/store — Spatz variant
#
# Spatz-specific alternative encodings for flb/fsb. Selected IN ADDITION to
# the rv_xsmallfloat_* files (which keep the Occamy/Snitch flb/fsb at
# funct3=0). See "Spatz variant extensions" in
# extensions/unratified/README.md for the rationale and retirement plan.
#
# Spatz hardware implements flb/fsb at funct3=4 (the pre-Occamy draft
# encoding):
# - funct3=0 at LOAD-FP is vle8.v space; in the Spatz snitch decoder
#   (unique casez) an flb pattern at funct3=0 would also match every
#   vle8.v word.
# - the post-increment loads (p.flb.rrpost in rv_xrrpost) are internally
#   re-encoded by the Spatz snitch core to a plain flb with funct3=4 on
#   the accelerator interface, and the FPU sequencer decodes that word
#   against this encoding.
#
# INFO: overlaps with rv_q (flq/fsq occupy funct3=4; Spatz has no Q)

flb.spatz  rd rs1 imm12 14..12=4 6..2=0x01 1..0=3
fsb.spatz  imm12hi rs1 rs2 imm12lo 14..12=4 6..2=0x09 1..0=3
